--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "notUsed",
      "forms": [],
      "description": "The line or entry is named in data (sourceKind and its identifiers); subject is not read."
    },
    "dataRequired": true,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "data.sourceKind + data.documentNo + data.lineNo",
      "form": "source kind, document no. and line no.",
      "description": "A sales, purchase, transfer or assembly line, by document number and line number."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.sourceKind + data.entryNo",
      "form": "item ledger entry no.",
      "description": "An item ledger entry, by its entry number."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.sourceKind + data.systemId",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The line or item ledger entry, by its SystemId."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "sourceKind",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Sales, Purchase, Transfer, Assembly or ItemLedgerEntry. Required."
    },
    {
      "name": "documentType",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Sales and Purchase: Quote, Order, Invoice, Credit Memo, Blanket Order or Return Order. Assembly: Quote, Order or Blanket Order. Defaults to Order. Not used for Transfer and ItemLedgerEntry."
    },
    {
      "name": "documentNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The document number of the line. Required for a line unless systemId is sent."
    },
    {
      "name": "lineNo",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The line number. Required for a line unless systemId is sent."
    },
    {
      "name": "systemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The SystemId of the line or item ledger entry. Do not send the other identifiers with it."
    },
    {
      "name": "entryNo",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The item ledger entry number. ItemLedgerEntry only. Required unless systemId is sent."
    },
    {
      "name": "direction",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Transfer only: Outbound (the shipment side, default) or Inbound (the receipt side)."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success when the chain was read; the list is empty when the line has no chain."
      },
      {
        "name": "sourceKind",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The source kind in its canonical spelling: Sales, Purchase, Transfer, Assembly or ItemLedgerEntry."
      },
      {
        "name": "entries",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "One row per link in the chain.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "level",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The level of the link in the chain; 1 is the line or entry you asked about."
          },
          {
            "name": "itemNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The item number of the link."
          },
          {
            "name": "quantity",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The tracked quantity of the link, in the base unit of measure."
          },
          {
            "name": "suppliedBy",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The supply, in words."
          },
          {
            "name": "demandedBy",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The demand, in words; CURRENT LINE marks the line you asked about."
          },
          {
            "name": "fromType",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The table number of the line or entry this link comes from."
          },
          {
            "name": "fromTypeName",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The name of that table."
          },
          {
            "name": "fromSubtype",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The subtype of the from line, for example the document type."
          },
          {
            "name": "fromNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The document or batch of the from line."
          },
          {
            "name": "fromLineNo",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The line or entry number of the from line."
          },
          {
            "name": "forType",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The table number of the line or entry on this level."
          },
          {
            "name": "forTypeName",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The name of that table."
          },
          {
            "name": "forSubtype",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The subtype of the for line, for example the document type."
          },
          {
            "name": "forNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The document or batch of the for line."
          },
          {
            "name": "forLineNo",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The line or entry number of the for line."
          },
          {
            "name": "shipmentDate",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The shipment date in YYYY-MM-DD form; blank when there is none."
          },
          {
            "name": "expectedReceiptDate",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The expected receipt date in YYYY-MM-DD form; blank when there is none."
          },
          {
            "name": "startingDate",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The starting date in YYYY-MM-DD form; blank when there is none."
          },
          {
            "name": "endingDate",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The ending date in YYYY-MM-DD form; blank when there is none."
          },
          {
            "name": "warning",
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "True when Business Central flags the link with a warning."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "sourceKind is missing, or the line or entry is not identified.",
      "fix": "Send sourceKind, and documentNo and lineNo, entryNo or systemId."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "sourceKind, documentType or direction has a value this type does not support, a key does not apply to the sourceKind, or the Reservations domain is turned off.",
      "fix": "Send a value from the parameters chapter and only the keys of that sourceKind, or turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "A key has the wrong JSON type.",
      "fix": "Send lineNo and entryNo as integers and systemId as a GUID."
    },
    {
      "code": "UnknownParameter",
      "when": "The request contains a key this type does not read.",
      "fix": "Remove the unknown key. Allowed keys are sourceKind, documentType, documentNo, lineNo, systemId, entryNo and direction."
    },
    {
      "code": "ConflictingIdentifiers",
      "when": "systemId was sent together with documentType, documentNo, lineNo or entryNo.",
      "fix": "Send systemId or the other identifiers, not both."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "No line or item ledger entry matches the identifiers.",
      "fix": "Check the document and line no."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller cannot read reservation entries or the source table.",
      "fix": "Assign the Bifrost \"Read-Only\" permission set (extended by Inventory read permissions) and a Business Central permission set that can read these tables."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "The native order tracking error text.",
      "when": "Business Central fails while it reads the chain; the answer carries its text.",
      "fix": "Read the error text and check the line it names."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "read",
    "changes": "Nothing is changed. The order tracking chain is worked out for the call and returned; no reservation is created or changed.",
    "idempotent": true,
    "permissionSet": "the Bifrost \"Read-Only\" permission set",
    "preconditions": [
      "The Reservations domain is turned on in Inventory Setup."
    ],
    "writes": false,
    "posts": false
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.AutoReserve",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Reserve a sales order line first, then read its tracking chain."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read the reservation entries themselves."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Read the tracking chain of a reserved sales order line",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.OrderTracking.Get",
        "data": {
          "sourceKind": "Sales",
          "documentType": "Order",
          "documentNo": "101005",
          "lineNo": 10000
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "sourceKind": "Sales",
        "entries": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "itemNo": "1000",
            "quantity": 2,
            "suppliedBy": "Item Ledger Entry 345",
            "demandedBy": "CURRENT LINE",
            "fromType": 32,
            "fromTypeName": "Item Ledger Entry",
            "fromSubtype": 0,
            "fromNo": "",
            "fromLineNo": 345,
            "forType": 37,
            "forTypeName": "Sales Line",
            "forSubtype": 1,
            "forNo": "101005",
            "forLineNo": 10000,
            "shipmentDate": "2026-10-20",
            "expectedReceiptDate": "",
            "startingDate": "2026-10-20",
            "endingDate": "2026-10-20",
            "warning": false
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Reads the order tracking chain for a sales, purchase, transfer or assembly line, or for one item ledger entry, as the Order Tracking page shows it. Each entry names the supply, the demand, the quantity and the dates. This call does not create or change reservations.",
  "notes": "Each entry is one link of the chain. for is the line or entry on that level, at level 1 the one you asked about, and from is the line or entry it is linked to. suppliedBy and demandedBy name the supply and the demand in words; CURRENT LINE marks the line you asked about. fromType and forType are table numbers, fromTypeName and forTypeName their names, fromNo and forNo the document or batch, fromLineNo and forLineNo the line or entry number, and quantity is in the base unit of measure. A line without reservations or order tracking answers an empty entries list, and so does a sales or purchase line that is not an item line. For Transfer, direction picks the shipment side (Outbound) or the receipt side (Inbound). Send only the keys that fit the sourceKind: documentType, documentNo and lineNo for Sales, Purchase and Assembly (documentType defaults to Order), documentNo, lineNo and direction for Transfer, entryNo for ItemLedgerEntry. systemId replaces the other identifiers. A key that does not fit the sourceKind is refused as InvalidParameter. The call only reads; the Reservations domain must be turned on in Inventory Setup."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
